<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.optionscalculator.ib-gateway</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__PROJECT_ROOT__/scripts/automation/run_ib_gateway.sh</string>
  </array>
  <!--
    IB Gateway, the ib_gateway options provider's data source: started at
    login and restarted whenever it exits. IB's daily auto-logoff may exit
    cleanly, so failure-only supervision can silently leave the production
    provider down. To stop it intentionally, unload/bootout the job rather than
    merely quitting the app. ThrottleInterval spaces restarts so a missing app
    retries every 30s instead of spinning.

    Login is still a person's job: the gateway comes back to its login
    window and the API port opens only after someone signs in. Unattended
    sign-in needs a third-party controller (IBC) holding the credentials,
    which this job deliberately does not do.

    A GUI application: Aqua-only so launchd never tries to start it in a
    headless session, and Interactive so the window server treats it like
    an app the user opened.
  -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>30</integer>
  <!--
    With IB's daily auto-restart on, the gateway relaunches itself as a child
    of the old process, still signed in, and the old process exits. By
    default launchd then kills everything left in the job's process group,
    which is that relaunched gateway. Abandon the group so it survives; the
    wrapper finds it on its next run and adopts it instead of starting a new
    one at the login window. Consequence: unloading the job stops the wrapper
    but leaves an adopted gateway running; quit that one from its own menu.
  -->
  <key>AbandonProcessGroup</key>
  <true/>
  <key>LimitLoadToSessionType</key>
  <string>Aqua</string>
  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Interactive</string>
  <!--
    Not *_launchd*.log: these stay open for the gateway's whole life, so the
    log rotation job must not rename them (it matches only *_launchd*.log).
  -->
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/.options_calculator_pro/logs/ib_gateway_stdout.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__HOME__/.options_calculator_pro/logs/ib_gateway_stderr.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
